  "verified": [
    "The same public package and source-change rejection/retry contracts pass over both authenticated transports on macOS and Linux.",
    "Explicit object watches never discover or recursively add paths. Reconciliation rechecks owned object metadata and registration changes require another matching complete inventory.",
    "Outside-root hard-link writes with restored contents and modification times, directory aliases, file replacements, cancellation cleanup and loss of coverage are covered by actual native tests.",
    "Linux inotify watches bind to owned O_PATH descriptors. Removing one hard-link registration preserves the shared inode watch until its last registration is removed.",
    "Unexpected Linux watch loss, queue overflow, truncated event data and unknown registrations reject coverage rather than publish a fresh observation.",
    "Partial registration-budget failure preserves the previous complete inventory and revision, closes partial descriptors, and permits one clean generation advance on retry.",
    "Git 2.39.5 nested-project staging preserves public project files while excluding runtime folders and case aliases; sibling files remain unstaged and staged siblings prevent a project-wide commit."
